bin
logs
wandb
outputs
data/*
# every novel-view sweep publishes (eval_log.json + rollout videos), so a new
# sweep needs no .gitignore edit; the multi-GB zarrs/checkpoints stay out
!data/eval_*/
!data/eval_*/**
# relational-probe (step 1a) outputs: one small JSON per checkpoint, and the JSON *is* the
# measurement artifact -- every number is re-derivable from it without re-running.
!data/probe_relpose_*/
!data/probe_relpose_*/**
# the single-view z_g decode (same probe, --stability-ranges "1,1"). PROGRESS.md's Stage 2
# of *the second failure mode* reads latent_grid["1,1"].zg_abs_pose straight out of these,
# and until 2026-09-25 NONE of them were tracked -- the Artifacts table in NOTES.md claimed
# otherwise, so a committed headline result rested on box-only files.
!data/probe_zg_*/
!data/probe_zg_*/**
# collapse screens (screen_collapse.py): one small JSON per checkpoint, ditto.
!data/screen_collapse/
!data/screen_collapse/**
# conditioning screens (screen_conditioning.py): ditto.
!data/screen_conditioning/
!data/screen_conditioning/**
# ring montages only -- data/multiview/ also holds the multi-GB zarrs
!data/multiview/
data/multiview/*
!data/multiview/*.png
!data/outputs/
data/outputs/*
!data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# M3 runs: the per-batch train/val/rollout curves, same rationale as M1's above.
# The 4.6 GB checkpoints stay out; only logs.json.txt (~9 MB/run) is published.
!data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_m3*_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# M4 runs: same rationale. logs.json.txt carries the aux_loss curve, which is the
# primary evidence that the aux mechanism is learnable (see the M4 section of PROGRESS.md).
!data/outputs/run_*_m4*_s42_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_m4*_s42_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_m4*_s42_200ep/logs.json.txt
# M1 re-train (2026-09-25): recovers the single-view baseline weights that were deleted
# 2026-09-19, so its ENCODER can be collapse-screened -- the question is whether the
# original baseline was itself collapsed. Same rule: logs only, never the checkpoints.
!data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_*200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_*200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_abs_single_*200ep/logs.json.txt
# L1 (randview) runs: the s43 seed-mate of L1 square was missed by the original whitelist,
# so one committed number's only training record was absent from git. L1's seed-robustness
# claim (collapse screens agree to 26% across s42/s43) rests on that run.
!data/outputs/run_*_randview_s*_200ep/
data/outputs/run_*_randview_s*_200ep/*
!data/outputs/run_*_randview_s*_200ep/logs.json.txt
